Falsifies `pci::verification::read_bars_is_total_for_any_device`.

The defect: the BAR loop runs one slot past the end, `i <= slots` in place of `i < slots`. An
endpoint has six BARs and both spellings look like "all of them" at a glance; the 64-bit branch's
two-slot step already makes the index arithmetic here non-obvious.

Expected to fail: the totality claim, as an out-of-bounds index on `out[i]` at `i == 6`. It
needs a device that reports an endpoint header and answers the size probe with a usable mask on
the seventh slot, which is exactly the arbitrary-response regime this harness quantifies over and
nothing a fixture supplies.

